    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Only `AcceptanceTest` exists as a test class (the others are support base classes), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners`: when a request repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is returned with 200 instead of creating a duplicate.\n\n**New files (each a small, single-method unit \u2014 minimal surrounding complexity):**\n- `IdempotencyStore.java` \u2014 a `@Component` holding a `ConcurrentHashMap<String,Integer>` mapping key \u2192 owner id.\n- `CheckIdempotency.java` \u2014 first pipeline step; reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. On a known key it takes a `@Flow(\"existing\")` branch passing the stored owner id; otherwise it publishes the key as `Out<String>` and continues.\n- `RecordIdempotency.java` \u2014 after `SaveOwner`, records key \u2192 new owner id.\n- `RespondWithExistingOwner.java` \u2014 the branch responder; loads the owner by id and sends it as `OwnerDto` (200 by default).\n\n**Edited:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 added `checkIdempotency` as the new entry step (with `outputs: { existing: respondExisting }`), the `respondExisting` step, and inserted `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `audit`.\n\nNo existing function class was modified \u2014 behaviour was added as cohesive new units wired in via YAML, so structural impact stays low. The `@RequestHeader(required=false)` binding (confirmed supported by the OfficeFloor Spring MVC argument integration) yields `null` when the header is absent, leaving the normal create path unchanged.",
