    "probe_text": "I've now read the full pipeline (`owners.POST.yml`), every function class it wires, the helpers they call, and the request DTO's bean-validation constraints. Here is the complete ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\nEverything below runs inside a **single `transaction` governance that spans the whole pipeline and commits once at the end** (so any escalation thrown mid-way rolls back).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `composition.authorize: hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`).\n\n## Ordered steps\n\n1. **CheckIdempotency** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (optional). If a key is present *and already recorded* in `IdempotencyStore`, it branches to **RespondWithExistingOwner** (re-loads that owner by id and returns it `200`) and the create stops here. If the key is present but unseen, it publishes the key for step 17. Note: this runs on the **header only, before body validation**.\n\n2. **ValidateRegistrationDate** \u2014 the *only* `@RequestBody` binding, so this is where **bean validation of `OwnerFieldsDto` fires** (\u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, 400):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 not null, size 1\u201330, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 not null, size 1\u201330, pattern `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n   - `city` \u2014 not null, non-blank, size 1\u201380\n   - `telephone` \u2014 not null, size 1\u201320\n   - `email` \u2014 optional, valid email, max 255\n   - `postcode` \u2014 optional, must match `^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` \u2014 non-blank, size 1\u2013255; `addressLine2`/`title` size caps\n   - Then a business check: if `registrationDate` is supplied and **after today**, throw `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Republishes the body as a variable.\n\n3. **BuildOwner** \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` (email lower-cased by `Owner.setEmail`), then mutates the entity:\n   - `StructuredAddress.apply` \u2014 normalizes/composes `address` from `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`) preferring the structured form.\n   - Normalizes `telephone` to **E.164**; invalid or wrong national length \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n   - Defaults `registrationDate` to today if absent, then **rolls it forward** off weekends/holidays via `BusinessDay.roll`.\n   - Publishes a `sharesHousehold` boolean.\n\n4. **RejectDisposableEmail** \u2014 if the email domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException` (400).\n\n5. **ValidatePostcode** \u2014 if a postcode is present *and* the city maps to a known region, reject when it's outside that region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). Absent postcode or unknown city passes.\n\n6. **AssignHousehold** *(mutation)* \u2014 sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n\n7. **EnsureUniqueHousehold** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold: true`, reject if that `householdId` already belongs to a non-deleted owner \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).\n\n8. **EnsureUniqueIdentity** \u2014 reject if the full identity key `telephone|email|householdId` equals a non-deleted owner's \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409).\n\n9. **AssignCustomerCode** *(mutation)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city, hash8 of `telephone+lastName`).\n\n10. **DeduplicateCustomerCode** *(mutation)* \u2014 if that code collides with any existing owner's, append `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 until unique.\n\n11. **CountNamesakes** *(mutation)* \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n12. **EnsureCityCapacity** \u2014 reject if the city already holds **\u2265 50** owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n13. **EnsureDailyLimit** \u2014 reject if **\u2265 100** owners already have today's (rolled) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (429).\n\n14. **FlagBulkSignup** *(mutation)* \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true when **> 80** owners already share today's registration date.\n\n15. **FlagPossibleDuplicate** *(mutation)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, sets `possibleDuplicate=true` + `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>` on the first existing owner in the same household with a *different* telephone; otherwise sets it false.\n\n16. **SaveOwner** *(side effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (the actual insert; generates the id).\n\n17. **RecordIdempotency** *(side effect)* \u2014 if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in `IdempotencyStore` for future replays.\n\n18. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side effect)* \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line: id, customerCode, registrationDate, derived membershipLevel and membershipNumber.\n\n19. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **`201 Created`** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Quick summary\n- **Rejections (validation), in order:** bean-validation of the body \u2192 future registration date \u2192 invalid telephone \u2192 disposable email \u2192 out-of-region postcode \u2192 duplicate household \u2192 duplicate identity \u2192 city at capacity (\u226550) \u2192 daily limit (\u2265100).\n- **Mutations that decorate the entity:** structured address, E.164 phone, business-day registration date, householdId, customerCode (+dedup), namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate flags.\n- **External side-effects:** DB save, idempotency record, audit log, `201` with Location \u2014 plus the short-circuit idempotent replay at step 1.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: the **idempotency lookup (step 1) runs before body bean-validation (step 2)**, and several \"reject\" checks (household, identity, city, daily limit) scan the whole repository via `findAll()` on each create."
